  "id": "Compound::DB01144 - Gene::768",
  "verbalization": "Diclofenamide is likely to interact with Ca9 through a series of biochemical pathways involving calcium-related activities. The evidence suggests that Diclofenamide binds to Ca14 or Ca5b, which then participate in processes such as reversible hydration of carbon dioxide or carbonate dehydratase activity. These processes are ultimately linked to Ca9, indicating a potential role for Diclofenamide in modulating calcium-dependent metabolic functions. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Diclofenamide may influence cellular processes involving calcium, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a dependency on calcium-related activities, suggesting a possible role in cellular homeostasis or metabolic regulation.",
